# OpenEVV sound map: Croatian (eSpeak NG voice zls/hr), spoken by openevv's Italian module
# with the sounds, the melody and the tones of the language itself.
# Written by engine/accent/mapwriter.py; OpenEvvFrontend reads it, and docs/LANGUAGES.md
# says what each line means. Edit freely: the file is read each time a voice starts.

template itix
style standard
vowels i e E a o c u
glides r l L y w
schwa e
secondary 0

# the melody: peak; a question that wants yes or no: fall
accent f0=own range=90 shape=0 accent=26 accent2=12 unstressed=-6 decl=8 declmax=30 fs=-18 fw=-12 fc=10 fe=-12 fq=-8 qreg=14 span=2 stressed=106 weak=94 stop=0

# the words a question is asked with, which is not the question that wants yes or no
whwords first ko tko šta što gde gdje kada kad
whwords first kako zašto koji koja koje koliko kuda kamo
whwords first čiji ко шта где када кад како зашто
whwords first који која које колико куда чији

# what the module says in place of a phone it is given
says C t S
says D d z
says J d Z
says T t s

